# The bootloader's build id: 8 characters in its info block (0x08000010), one per bootloader code, so that boards
# with the same id run the same bootloader. The rule: a new id (a date, never used before) when, and only when, the
# bootloader's code changes (anything that changes bl.bin besides the id); then the md5 below with it.
# bootloader/build_bl.sh and tools/build_release.sh read the id here (BL_BUILD_ID=... overrides it for a test build).
# build_release.sh stops when the bootloader it built doesn't match its md5 here: the code changed without a new id.
# The md5: bl.bin built with xPack GCC 15.2 (tools/toolchain), the upper-records layout (the default), per board
# revision: rev<N> the dig2analog-ultra-5ch's (hardware 1), hw2-rev<N> the Diff-Power Ultra-Analog receiver's
# (hardware 2, BL_HW_ID=2; round 11: tools/build_release.sh RX=1), hw3-rev<N> the Diff-Power Ultra-Digital receiver's
# (hardware 3, BL_HW_ID=3: BLANK_N LOW from the first instruction, a marker before a frame skipped; its own code only: hw 1 / 2
# unchanged; UD=1).
